messages:
sam: quick q — we have an umbrella chart that needs to optionally mount a secret and set an env var only if the secret exists in the target namespace. wanted to avoid failing deploys when the secret is absent and keep a sane default in values.yaml. any patterns people use for conditional secret mounts + env fallback?

alex: two quick approaches i've used: 1) make the secret mount conditional in the template (`if .Values.someSecret.enabled`) and document that infra must set it; 2) runtime lookup of the secret with `lookup` and then render the env var only if lookup found something.

jamie: example of `lookup` approach i keep in a helper:
```yaml
{{- $s := lookup "v1" "Secret" .Release.Namespace "my-secret-name" -}}
{{- if $s }}
env:
  - name: MY_SECRET_KEY
    valueFrom:
      secretKeyRef:
        name: my-secret-name
        key: key
{{- else }}
env:
  - name: MY_SECRET_KEY
    value: "" # fallback if secret missing
{{- end }}
```
This keeps deploys non-fatal.

priya: small gotcha — `helm lint` will complain about `lookup` in some CI setups because lint doesn't contact a k8s cluster unless you run with `--kube-version` shim or use a chart-testing job that uses a real cluster. so add a note to our lint pipeline.

sam: thanks — do we prefer the values flags approach or lookup for cross-region deployments where secret name changes (we have external-secret naming conventions per region)?

alex: if secret name varies per environment, use a value like `secretName: ""` with override in values for each overlay and keep the template tolerant: `if .Values.secretName | trim | ne ""` then mount, else try `lookup` as fallback.

priya: helper that combines both: 
```yaml
{{- define "mychart.resolveSecret" -}}
{{- $name := .Values.secretName -}}
{{- if and (typeIs "string" $name) (ne (trim $name) "") -}}
  {{- $name -}}
{{- else -}}
  {{- $found := lookup "v1" "Secret" .Release.Namespace "external-secret-{{ .Release.Namespace }}" -}}
  {{- if $found }}{{- printf "%s" $found.metadata.name -}}{{- else -}}{{- "" -}}{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
```
Then call it and if result is empty skip mount and set empty env.

jamie: also add schema to `values.schema.json` for `secretName` as nullable string so editors/CI tell users what's expected.

sam: tried the helper locally, helm template worked. ran into helmfile chart-testing job failing earlier — looks like our chart-testing cluster doesn't have the external-secret created so the `lookup` returns nil and our logic is fine, but some downstream e2e expected the env to be present. i'll update the tests to allow empty fallback.

devops-bot: ci/cd:chart-testing started for branch fix/optional-secret-fallback — job #412 queued

alex: once CI green, can we add a short README note in chart root about the `secretName` override vs lookup fallback? tiny doc helps infra teams.

priya: +1. also add a lint-exception note for `lookup` in our dev checklist.

sam: will do. thanks all :thumbsup:
